"""Bzlmod root module for the Qorix Engineering repo.

This repo is currently docs-only from Bazel's point of view (no BUILD.bazel
targets exist yet — content is Sphinx/Sphinx-Needs .rst, Python, Rust via
Cargo, etc.). This file's only job is to mark the repo root as a Bazel
workspace so `bazel build //...` / `bazel test //...` (run by
.github/workflows/ci.yml's bazel-build-test job) can execute at all instead
of failing with:

    ERROR: The 'build' command is only supported from within a workspace
    (below a directory having a MODULE.bazel file).

With no BUILD.bazel files anywhere in the tree, `//...` currently expands
to an empty target set, so build/test both succeed trivially (0 targets).
When real Bazel targets are added under any subdirectory, add their
dependencies as bazel_dep() entries below.
"""

module(
    name = "qorix_engineering",
    version = "0.0.0",
)
